# TypeScript SDK

Use the TypeScript SDK when your agent runs in Node.js, a Next.js route handler, or a worker. Keep instrumentation at the boundary of a request so every downstream operation remains connected.

## Install and configure

```bash
npm install tracify-sdk
```

```ts
import { Tracify } from "tracify-sdk";

const tracify = new Tracify({ apiKey: process.env.TRACIFY_API_KEY });
```

## Trace model and tool work

```ts
await tracify.trace("research-agent", async (trace) => {
  const context = await trace.span("retrieval", () => searchDocs(question));
  return trace.span("llm.call", () => callModel({ question, context }));
});
```

Use session and release fields to compare runs across customers and deployments. Never expose a project API key in browser code.
